# These files are executed or parsed on Linux, so they must keep LF endings
# whatever the checkout platform does. On Windows core.autocrlf=true rewrites
# them to CRLF, and git archive applies the same conversion — which produced a
# deployment tarball whose scripts died immediately with
#   bootstrap.sh: line 12: $'\r': command not found
#   bootstrap.sh: line 13: set: pipefail: invalid option name
# because the carriage return becomes part of the shebang and of every command.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
